		"shapes": "Additive deltas, not absolute poses: bones a characteristic leaves alone are identity in both of its clips, so they are omitted, and only the channels that differ between min and max are listed. Apply after the animation mixer, per characteristic value v in 0..1: position += lerp(tMin, tMax, v); quaternion = quaternion * slerp(rMin, rMax, v) (post-multiply); scale *= lerp(sMin, sMax, v). Translations are metres in the bone parent space, the same space as the GLB node translations. Quaternions are [x, y, z, w], signed so rMin.w >= 0 and dot(rMin, rMax) >= 0. Bone names are the GLB node names. On the shipped data every rotation delta sits on an *_ENV helper whose bind and animated rotation are identity, and every scaled bone has unit scale in the idle clips, so only the translation composition (neck_2, head, wing_2_*, the *_ENV offsets) actually interacts with the animation.",
		"presets": "The ranges each characteristic is rolled in per life stage, [min, max] in 0..1. The presets name a 'comb' that no characteristic is called (those are comb_front and comb_back); how the game maps it is not in the data.",
		"matgrpWeights": "chicken_metadata.matgrps, only the entries that carry a freq. Groups listed without one (and groups not listed) are omitted: their weight is unknown, treat it as 0 for rolls. Group indices are material group indices, the same as materialGroups[].index.",
		"seedExpressions": "Normalised VfxEval source (vfxeval.ts), identical in meaning to VRF master's decompile: every binary operation, conditional and &&/|| is bracketed; comparisons give 0 or 1; a && b is a ? b : 0 and a || b is a ? 1 : b; % is float modulo; float2() builds a vector and arithmetic is per component; lines are joined by a space. Keys naming a texture slot (g_t*) come from m_dynamicTextureParams; the engine's use of their value is not known.",
		"features": "Raw F_* ints from the vmat. F_DETAIL_TEXTURE: absent or 0 = Multiply, 1 = Replace (csgo_character features VCS).",
		"textures": "CDN paths. Textures under materials/models/ ship in the pettex root; materials/default/* are the shared engine defaults the defaults job already publishes, so they point there."
